We are looking for an Accounting Methodology & Automation Manager to join our Finance team and support the Group's ERP implementation and ongoing business transformation.
In this role, you will work at the intersection of accounting, finance, business and IT. You will translate business requirements and changes into accounting methodology, define how accounting processes should work in ERP and 1C, and collaborate with developers and business analysts to automate them.
Job Responsibilities

• Develop and maintain accounting methodology for the Group's business models, including merchant and agency models (net / gross), prepayment and postpayment, B2B and B2C transactions across hotels, air, rail, transfers and ancillary services;

• Design accounting rules, posting logic and chart-of-accounts requirements, defining the data needed to automate accounting processes in ERP and 1C;

• Translate business scenarios, new products and process changes into accounting requirements and technical specifications for developers and business analysts;

• Define data sources, field mappings, document flows and reconciliation logic, including the handling of corrections and disputes;

• Collaborate with IT, product teams, business analysts and other stakeholders to implement and improve accounting processes;

• Ensure that automated accounting entries are aligned with supplier and partner settlements, as well as intercompany balances;

• Analyse the accounting implications of new products, contracts and system changes under IFRS, with a particular focus on IFRS 15;

• Design and improve intercompany accounting and settlement processes between Group entities;

• Support ERP implementation and rollout to new entities, including accounting methodology, migration rules and process standardisation;

• Review supplier, partner and intercompany contracts from an accounting and VAT perspective, identifying potential improvements to invoicing and payment processes;

• Support operational accountants on methodological matters and perform user acceptance testing (UAT) of automated accounting processes before go-live.

Requirements

• A degree in Accounting, Finance, Economics or a related field;

• At least 5 years of experience in accounting, including 2+ years in accounting methodology, accounting process automation or accounting systems implementation;

• Solid knowledge of IFRS, particularly IFRS 15, including revenue recognition and principal-versus-agent considerations;

• Practical experience working with ERP systems or 1C, with an understanding of accounting logic, posting rules and document flows - beyond day-to-day system usage;

• Experience translating business requirements into accounting methodology and technical specifications for developers or business analysts;

• Understanding of how accounting processes and data flows are organised and automated across different systems;

• Practical experience with SQL or writing queries to retrieve and analyse data would be an advantage;

• Understanding of APIs and system integrations;

• Strong analytical skills and confidence working with large data sets in Excel, including pivot tables and lookup functionsl

• Ability to work independently, manage project timelines and deliver results;

• Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain complex accounting matters to both finance and technical teams;

• Language proficiency: Upper-Intermediate English (B2) or higher; other languages are a plus.

Benefits

• Flexible schedules and opportunity to work remotely;

• Ambitious and supportive team who love what they do, appreciate each other, and grow together;

• Internal programs for adaptation and training, development of soft skills, and leadership abilities;

• Partial compensation for participating in external training and conferences;

• Corporate English school: Group and individual lessons, speaking clubs with colleagues from all over the world;

• Corporate prices on hotels and travel

Position: Compliance Data Specialist
Status: Full-Time
FLSA Code: Non-Exempt
Please note: This position is with AccredTech, Verified First ’s sister company. While this posting is listed through Verified First , the role works for AccredTech.
About Us
AccredTech is a fast-growing compliance technology company on a mission to make DOT and FMCSA driver qualification simple, accurate, and audit-ready. As a sister company to Verified First , we share the same belief: we work hard to play hard. We’re a bunch of goal-setters who dream big and win bigger. When you’re part of the AccredTech team, you can be sure we’ll invest in you as both a professional and a human. We’re looking for people like you (detail-driven, hard-working, and a little goofy) to join our team!
Summary
The Compliance Data Specialist is responsible for delivering AccredTech’s managed service to our clients by keeping their driver qualification files complete, accurate, and current. This includes moving screening results and supporting data from Verified First into the AccredTech platform, assigning and flagging documents, and corresponding with clients according to each client’s defined process. Additionally, the role involves performing account, user, and API setup for clients and helping the business identify processes and notifications that can be automated. This position ensures our managed service clients receive a reliable, hands-off compliance experience.
How our Compliance Data Specialist spends their time

• Data transfer (60%): Move background screening results, driver records, and supporting documents from Verified First into the AccredTech platform accurately and on time, verifying data integrity at each step;

• Document management (10%): Assign documents to the correct driver files and requirements, and flag missing, expired, incomplete, or non-compliant items for follow-up;

• Client communication (10%): Alert and correspond with clients as needed, following each client’s specified process for notifications, escalations, and approvals;

• Process improvement and automation (10%): Help inform the business by identifying repetitive tasks, recurring issues, and notification gaps, and partner with Product and Development to automate specific processes and notifications;

• Account setup (10%): Perform account, user, and API setup for clients as needed, ensuring configurations match client requirements;

• Perform other duties as assigned.

What you bring

• Ability to maintain regular and punctual attendance;

• Ability to communicate effectively, including the ability to manage client expectations and resolve conflict professionally;

• Ability to be held accountable to department and organizational numbers, data, and deadlines;

• Ability to quickly pivot, be process-oriented, with high attention to detail and data accuracy;

• Ability to manage high-volume, repetitive work while maintaining quality and consistency;

• Demonstrate and promote non-negotiable integrity and dignity of the individual in an environment of mutual trust and respect;

• Maintain discretion in working with sensitive and confidential information, including driver and personally identifiable information (PII);

• Exhibit a commitment to lifelong learning, encourage others to do so, and continue to grow technically and interpersonally to perform the job at the highest levels of competency;

• Demonstration of a servant-leadership mindset toward all, evidenced by client satisfaction;

• Encourage a direct and positive relationship between community and company.

Preferred Qualifications

• High School Diploma or equivalent required. Associate’s or Bachelor’s Degree preferred;

• Minimum of 1 year of experience in data entry, records management, compliance administration, or a similar detail-oriented role;

• Knowledge of DOT/FMCSA driver qualification file (DQF) requirements (49 CFR Part 391) preferred;

• Knowledge of the background screening industry and products preferred;

